"Old Man" (Placeholder/Mabel): Let's finish this strory once and for all stranger..
"Old Man": Everyone answered "Yes" to the Artist's question
"Old Man": He then decided to tell everyone a story,
"Old Man": His story of when he was in the same predicament as them
"Old Man": He said
"Old Man": When he was deciding whether to go Vienna or to Linz to become a master of art,
"Old Man": He was torn between the two and couldn't decide which would make him a master
"Old Man": Then a friend asked him
"Old Man": Why does it matter which city you go to?
"Old Man": Can you see yourself becoming a master if you choose either one of the cities?
"Old Man": If yes then the city does not matter what matters is "You"
"Old Man": That's when the Artist realised
"Old Man": That we always try to find the circumstances that can make us great
"Old Man": We put the circumstance's ability to affect our life above than our own
"Old Man": But the reality is if you dont believe in yourself then even the circumstances won't save you
"Old Man": But if you do
"Old Man": Then the circumstances do not matter, what makes you great is you yourself and "Your Hands"
"Old Man": So did you like this story stranger?
"Old Man": Now you should understand that you always need to believe in the path you choose
"Old Man": Now i have one Final question for you
